How the internet really works behind the scenes?

Here’s a simple breakdown of the 6 core server types that power almost every digital service we use today. 
💡 Server Types Simplified:

1. 🌐 Origin Server – Serves the original content via edge/CDN.


2. 🧭 DNS Server – Translates domain names into IP addresses.


3. 📁 File Server – Stores and shares files across networks.


4. 📬 Mail Server – Manages sending and receiving of emails.


5. 🖥 Web Server – Delivers websites and web applications.


6. 🛡 Proxy Server – Protects and optimizes client-server requests.



💼 Used in Real-World Services:

AWS: EC2, Route 53, S3, SES

